{
    "background_story": "Malcolm was a renowned archaeologist who had spent his entire career studying the ancient civilizations of Africa. His latest obsession was the mysterious Likuta tribe, a long-lost culture known for their advanced knowledge of astronomy and mathematics. Malcolm's fascination with the Likuta led him to embark on a perilous expedition to the depths of the Congo jungle, where he hoped to uncover the remnants of their lost city. After months of trekking through the dense foliage, Malcolm finally stumbled upon an ancient temple hidden deep within the jungle. As he carefully excavated the site, he discovered a series of intricate carvings and artifacts that shed new light on the Likuta's remarkable achievements. Malcolm's groundbreaking discovery sparked a new wave of interest in the Likuta tribe, cementing his reputation as a leading expert in the field.",
